factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 5 problems
  The article says the Highways department itself said the concrete signboard cannot be demolished and rebuilt; the draft's reel_script and slides say the department 'vaithullathu' (placed the board) and the reel says officials said it's impossible — this is consistent, but the slides/reel omit that the Collector asked Highways whether the board could be extended, which is fine; however the reel_script claims the board is at the end of the bridge where 'signboard' location is misdescribed as 'அருகே' rather than at the bridge exit, minor.
  The reel_script states the Collector ordered removal of roadside encroachment and closure of the median gap, but the article only says he 'instructed' (அறிவுறுத்தினார) — acceptable; however the slide 'அதிகாரிகள் உத்தரவு' title attributes an order to officials while the article's order came from the Collector, which is a mixed attribution.
